# TaptPay — Product Brief (for design)

## What TaptPay is
TaptPay (a.k.a. "Tapt") is a **software-only payment terminal** that turns any
smartphone or tablet into a full EFTPOS replacement — no hardware to buy, install,
or maintain. Merchants accept payments two ways:

- **QR code** — the customer scans with any phone camera and pays.
- **NFC "tap to phone"** — the customer taps their phone or contactless card
  directly on the merchant's device. Supports **Apple Pay, Google Pay, Samsung
  Pay, and contactless cards**, with feature detection and graceful fallback.

Every transaction updates in **real time** (Server-Sent Events) on both the
merchant and customer screens. Payments settle through **Windcave** (PCI-DSS
compliant hosted payment page); TaptPay is the Merchant of Record.

**Platform:** iOS, Android, and web browser. Built as a React/TypeScript app.

---

## Why it stands out (vs traditional EFTPOS and competitors)
1. **No hardware.** Runs on phones/tablets the business already owns — no terminal
   purchase, rental, or maintenance.
2. **Lower fees.** Retail is **3.4% total (2.9% Windcave + 0.5% platform)** vs the
   typical 4–6% of legacy terminals — merchants keep ~96.6% of revenue. No monthly
   fees; pay only per transaction.
3. **Instant setup.** Start accepting payments in minutes, not weeks.
4. **Real-time everything.** Live transaction status, push notifications on
   created/completed/failed/refunded, instant analytics.
5. **Built for how people actually pay now** — digital wallets and tap, not just
   chip-and-pin.
6. **Multi-vertical.** One platform, purpose-built flows for very different
   businesses (see below) — not a one-size-fits-all terminal.

---

## The three verticals
TaptPay isn't a single app — it's one payments engine with **three tailored
verticals**, switchable per merchant.

### 1. Retail
The classic point-of-sale flow for cafés, shops, food trucks, and markets.
- Keypad/terminal to charge an amount, stock/product management, transaction
  history and analytics dashboard.
- **Split the bill** — merchant enables it; the customer divides the total
  between 2–10 people at pay time, each getting their own card flow and receipt.
- Professional receipts: itemised, full business details, **NZ GST (15%)**
  breakdown, PDF download + native share.

### 2. Property Management
Rent and recurring-invoice collection for landlords / property managers.
- Rent invoices with **recurring automation** (scheduled sends), plus an
  **overdue-reminder engine** (configurable delay, interval, and max count).
- Hosted checkout links customers pay via card; invoices settle idempotently and
  mark paid automatically.
- Same real-time + receipt + split-bill machinery as retail.

### 3. Trades (newest vertical)
For plumbers, electricians, builders — a quote-to-completion lifecycle.
- **Lifecycle:** quote → accept → deposit → balance → complete. An accepted quote
  becomes a *job* that parks in a home "stack".
- **Two paths:** a full **Quote builder** and a **quick Invoice** (keypad → send,
  no quote step).
- **Deposit link** auto-presented to the customer the instant they accept a
  deposit-enabled quote; the **balance** is a second payment link off the job.
- **Recurring toggle** for maintenance/retainer work.
- **Split the balance** supported here too.
- NZ **GST-inclusive** by default ("GST (15%) incl."), gated by the merchant's
  GST-registered flag.
- Low platform fee (0.3%).

---

## Feature highlights (cross-cutting)
- **QR + NFC tap-to-phone** payment acceptance.
- **Split the bill** — merchant-gated; customer divides at pay time (retail,
  property, and trades).
- **Real-time transaction feed** via SSE.
- **Web push notifications** for transaction status changes.
- **Refunds** with dedicated flow and real-time notifications.
- **Professional receipts** — full business info, NZ GST, PDF + share.
- **Multi-"stone" support** — multiple isolated payment endpoints per merchant.
- **Admin/merchant dashboards** — revenue, transactions, analytics.
- **Security** — JWT auth, per-merchant ownership checks, rate limiting, audit
  logging, PCI-DSS-compliant processing via Windcave.

---

## Audience & positioning
- Small-to-medium businesses wanting to ditch bulky, expensive EFTPOS.
- Cost-conscious merchants (cafés, retail, markets, tradespeople, landlords).
- Modern, mobile-first operators and pop-ups needing flexible payments.

**Tone:** professional yet approachable, results-focused (cost savings +
efficiency), technology-forward but jargon-free, trust-building on security.

---

## One-paragraph elevator pitch
> TaptPay turns any phone or tablet into a modern payment terminal — customers pay
> by scanning a QR code or tapping their phone or card (Apple Pay, Google Pay,
> Samsung Pay, contactless). No hardware, no monthly fees, and lower processing
> costs than traditional EFTPOS, with real-time transaction updates and instant
> analytics. And it's not one-size-fits-all: purpose-built verticals for **Retail**,
> **Property Management**, and **Trades** mean the flow fits the business — from a
> café splitting a bill, to a landlord automating rent, to a plumber quoting a job
> and collecting a deposit.
